# =========================================================================
# RFI Answer Builder — .gitignore
# =========================================================================
# Load-bearing for proprietary data containment. This file is committed
# BEFORE any other file in the repo, so nothing sensitive can slip in
# before the rules are in place.

# --- Proprietary RFI data (the reason this repo is private) -------------
# Real RFI spreadsheets / source docs from clients. Never committed.
#
# Broad rule (not just rfi_*.xlsx) because client-supplied filenames
# carry client names, dates, and internal codes — they will NOT match a
# tidy naming convention (e.g. "Utiq_Publicis RFI.xlsx", "INTERNAL -
# Reach Customer facing DPIA questions.xlsx"). Ignore every spreadsheet
# and source document in data/ by default; the fake demo file is the
# only exception.
data/*.xlsx
data/*.xls
data/*.csv
data/*.pdf
data/*.docx
# The fake sample (created later for safe demos) is the only exception.
!data/sample_rfi.xlsx

# --- Experiment outputs (may contain real RFI content) -------------------
# Validation runs, eval results, retrieval traces — all can incidentally
# capture proprietary question/answer text.
outputs/

# --- Per-file configs ----------------------------------------------------
# config_rfi_*.json holds column mappings + client/date metadata extracted
# at profile time. Client/date strings are sensitive; ignore them all.
# A sanitised sample config can be committed by name if needed later.
config_rfi_*.json

# --- Secrets -------------------------------------------------------------
# Mistral API key lives here. NEVER commit.
.env
.env.*
*.key
# The template (no real key) IS committed so a fresh clone knows what to set.
!.env.example

# --- Vector store (large, machine-specific, regenerable) -----------------
# ChromaDB persists here; ingest.py rebuilds it. May contain embedded
# proprietary chunk text — extra reason not to commit.
chroma_db/
*.sqlite3

# --- Python --------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/

# --- UI layer (rfi_SPEC.md) -----------------------------------------------
# Per-session uploads, profiles, configs, answers, outputs live here.
# Cleaned up by the backend on a 24h schedule. Never commit — the files
# include uploaded RFIs and generated answers.
tmp/

# Frontend build artefacts and node_modules. Big, machine-specific,
# regenerable via `npm install` + `npm run build` from package.json.
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/

# --- Claude Code local settings (machine-specific) ----------------------
.claude/settings.local.json

# --- OS / editor noise ---------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/